<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  ⚠️ PLACEHOLDER FIREBASE CONFIG — DO NOT SHIP ⚠️

  This file is a stand-in so the Xcode project builds out of the box.
  It does NOT point at a real Firebase project. Before running the app:

    1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com and create (or open) your
       "Nodi" project.
    2. Add an iOS app with bundle ID: com.nodinetwork.Nodi
       (must match `bundleIdPrefix` + target name in project.yml, or
       whatever bundle ID you set there).
    3. Download the real GoogleService-Info.plist Firebase generates for you.
    4. Replace this file at Nodi/Resources/GoogleService-Info.plist with it.
    5. In the Firebase console, enable: Authentication (Apple, Google,
       Email/Password providers), Firestore, Storage, Cloud Messaging,
       and Cloud Functions.
    6. Deploy firestore.rules, storage.rules, and firestore.indexes.json
       (see README → "Firebase Setup").
    7. Deploy the Cloud Functions in /functions (see functions/README.md).

  Until you do this, FirebaseApp.configure() in AppDelegate will either
  crash at launch or silently fail to authenticate/sync — that is expected
  with a placeholder config.
-->
